sion of 1.52x.","Operating margin is running 8pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.4x net debt to EBITDA ($69.2M of cash against $569.1M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 3.5x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.21)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -10.2% over 3 years, 11.6% over 5 years and 7.7% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 23%).","Margins are contracting (-1.7% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.99, a backlog worth 1% of annual revenue and deferred revenue down 44%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (8.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 26, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 54%.","It returns 13.2% a year to shareholders (13.2% in dividends).","It pays out 144% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 320 employees, each generates about $1.9M of revenue, 3.0x the Basic Materials median, and productivity has risen 5.1% a year.","That works out to $309K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.9M (1x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $31K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":68,"head":"Watch: operating margin contracting 1.7%/yr.","pros":["FCF margin 16.3%","Revenue grew 11.6%/yr over 5y","P/E 10.9x vs sector 16.5x","P/FCF 11.7x vs sector 22.8x","12-1 month momentum +43%"],"cons":["Operating margin contracting 1.7%/yr"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","only 5% below fair value"],"buy_below":97.61,"vc":{"base":114.83,"base_src":"dcf","bear":86.33,"bull":154.58,"alt_median":216.37,"n_alt":1,"gap":-0.4693,"dispersion":0.3066,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (31% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe"